Z||000009||Hartz||07-07-2001||01:48 PM||||OK, thanks everyone.  Specs on the turbo:  This car was completed back in 1995. It is based on a turbo kit that was originally purchased from Fiero Conversions, but we junked about half of it. I did use the turbo, the PROM, and some of the fittings. <P>The engine's been balanced and blueprinted.  It's got a valve job, ported cylinder heads, port matched intake and exhaust ports, etc. etc.  We threw in a Crane cam and lifters, a custom fab air intake, the GM 3.1 crank, custom JE forged pistons, the MSD 6BTM box with Accel Super Coil and 8.8 plug wires.  We beefed up the TH125 a bit, put a mandrel bent 2.5" exhaust under it, and ended it with a single SuperTrapp.<P>Believe it or not, I've never had it to the strip or dyno.  Gotta fix that here real soon.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Seat of the pants tells me it's not even close to being as quick as my V8 car, which runs 13.3.  I'm only running 6-8 lbs. of boost right now (no intercooler yet) so I'm guessing it's MAYBE a high 14 second car?  That's a big guess.<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<P><BR>||||reg||1
